   "daf": "71a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "אֵינוֹ נַעֲשֶׂה בֵּן סוֹרֵר וּמוֹרֶה עַד שֶׁיֹּאכַל בָּשָׂר וְיִשְׁתֶּה יַיִן. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: אָכַל כׇּל מַאֲכָל וְלֹא אָכַל בָּשָׂר, שָׁתָה כׇּל מַשְׁקֶה וְלֹא שָׁתָה יַיִן – אֵינוֹ נַעֲשֶׂה בֵּן סוֹרֵר וּמוֹרֶה עַד שֶׁיֹּאכַל בָּשָׂר וְיִשְׁתֶּה יַיִן, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״זוֹלֵל וְסֹבֵא״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the boy «does not become a stubborn and rebellious son unless he» actually «eats meat and drinks wine. The Sages taught» in a baraita: If «he ate any» other «food but did not eat meat,» or if «he drank any» other «beverage but did not drink wine, he does not become a stubborn and rebellious son unless he» actually «eats meat and drinks wine, as it is stated:» “This son of ours is stubborn and rebellious; he will not obey our voices; he is «a glutton and a drunkard.”»"
  }
 ],
